  "description": "UFARUR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H106 N4 O52 Sm6 Zn6,C1 H4 O1,4.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Sm1B (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2B (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3B (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1B (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn2B (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3B (Zn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.477-3.956 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.26-115.47°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C102H106N4O52Sm6Zn6·CH4O·4.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 18 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
